Known-answer vectors.  tests/vectors.rkt checks the hashes below.

rfc6979-nonces.rktd
  The seven test_rfc6979 rows (secret, message, nonce) of trezor-firmware
  crypto/tests/test_check.c at commit e22d597d27b3f57297d7a3d36a3b97b4ca5c09b1,
  https://github.com/trezor/trezor-firmware/blob/e22d597d27b3f57297d7a3d36a3b97b4ca5c09b1/crypto/tests/test_check.c
  Rows 1 and 2 are RFC 6979 A.2.5's key with "sample".
  Extracted by hand: for each of the seven cases, the private key, the
  message and the expected nonce as test_rfc6979 gives them, written as one
  (nonce-row secret message nonce) form per case in file order.
  Licence: MIT (trezor-crypto), trezor-crypto/LICENSE.
  Read by tests/ecdsa.rkt and tests/load.rkt.

tiny-secp256k1/ecdsa.json
  bitcoinjs/tiny-secp256k1 tests/fixtures/ecdsa.json, verbatim, at commit
  17d82c7fe38239d3ba0451202895837885f80e1c,
  https://github.com/bitcoinjs/tiny-secp256k1/blob/17d82c7fe38239d3ba0451202895837885f80e1c/tests/fixtures/ecdsa.json
  Licence: MIT, tiny-secp256k1/LICENSE.
  Read by tests/ecdsa.rkt, tests/cast.rkt, tests/concurrency.rkt and tests/load.rkt.

wycheproof/ecdsa_secp256k1_sha256_bitcoin_test.json
  Copied from the libsecp256k1 v0.8.0 tarball's src/wycheproof/, which took it from
  Wycheproof at commit 7ae4532f417575ced2b1cbbabed81a7fecfaef5d,
